2026-11-07T11:51:10.5952556Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5963495Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5964449Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5964930Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5965273Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5965621Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5965916Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5966144Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5966629Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5967236Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5967505Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5967984Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5968314Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5968632Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5969224Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-07T11:51:10.5969394Z 
